# Phase 4, GA-2-12's recheck (2026-10-14): a sub-row a bill has set can be put back. A drag within half the knob's step of the statute's figure
# leaves that figure exactly (the knob's detent, LedgerRow.Snap, and GameController.DragSubRow - the pension-age dial's half-a-month idiom, the statute taken as far as the track reaches it); the bill names a sub-row only where its
# draft moves the line (BuildBudgetBillFromDrafts); the merge reads the statute's own figure as the statute standing, and a line with no rate
# of its own left carries none (ParliamentSystem.MergedBracketRates). The repro (X-02R in the five countries whose income tax responds, on the
# 1280 step, the widest film's and exact) and the finding's area, 2. Expected: each X-02R run parts from its p4_ga2_12_pre or _pre2 twin on
# the day its restore bill passes - the TAXES line drops its brackets, the BURDEN gap returns to the seed's - wherever the restore passes;
# X-02R alternates while it can (the floor at a window, the restore at the next after one has passed); every area-2 run byte-identical to
# its p4_ga211 twin (no run there sets a sub-row; s827's cabinet copy is inert).
#
